      "id": 229024,
      "name": "Rabit",
      "username": "Rabit",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/{size}/7330_2.png",
      "created_at": "2019-10-22T11:58:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"MindWanderer\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/48/4816_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> MindWanderer:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Technically speaking, it’s “Add a Presence to a land within 3 of your existing Presence that has either Wilds or your Presence.”  Currently it’s redundant to require that it be both on your Presence and within 3 of your Presence, but there could in theory be an effect that made it a meaningful distinction.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I don’t agree that it’s redundant. If there are no wilds out, this allows you to place a presence at range of 0, where you have presence, because of the “or your presence” part. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>",
